    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Guinea pigs, <i>Cavia</i> <i>porcellus</i>, vary in the length and colour of their fur.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Fig. 1.1 shows a guinea pig with short black fur.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "figure",
        "id": "fig1.1",
        "caption": "Fig. 1.1",
        "src": "figures/q1_fig1_1.png",
        "alt": "Guinea pigs",
        "source": {
          "qp": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Two genes that determine the length and colour of the fur occur at the <b>A</b>/<b>a</b> locus and the <b>B</b>/<b>b</b> locus. These two gene loci are on separate autosomal chromosomes.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 2
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "The allele <b>A</b> results in short fur.",
          "The allele <b>a</b> results in long fur.",
          "<b>A</b> is dominant to <b>a</b>.",
          "The allele <b>B</b> results in black fur.",
          "The allele <b>b</b> results in chocolate fur.",
          "<b>B</b> is dominant to <b>b</b>."
        ]
      }
    ],
